WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.040
One of the busiest 24 hours of news in a long
time, so let's get right into it.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.040
We had democratic

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:12.210
presidential debate number seven last night
and it was the most shameful one so far in

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:16.600
terms of the hosting and the anchoring done
yesterday by CNN.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:21.660
Of course, as you probably now know, CNN on
Monday published this exclusive report about

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:27.060
how Bernie Sanders in 2018 supposedly told
Elizabeth Warren that a woman can't win the

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:36.059
presidency, and then there was the pretext
of that used to create drama during the debate

00:00:36.059 --> 00:00:40.239
exactly as I predicted would be done and in
general we'll get to that.

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:46.749
But in general, CNN filled the debate with
baiting questions and split screens, trying

00:00:46.749 --> 00:00:49.019
to get people to fight.

00:00:49.019 --> 00:00:53.010
Basically nobody took the bait and that was
actually a good decision by the candidates.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:58.539
They wasted time with these open ended questions
like what makes you qualified to be president,

00:00:58.539 --> 00:01:03.629
which at this late stage of the game, just
weeks before the first votes are lame, worthless

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:05.330
West waste of time.

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:06.330
Questions.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:12.900
CNN wrote a follow up questions in advance,
which makes sense to have, but the questions

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.150
ignored the candidates actual answers.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:24.170
So the debate was filled with followup questions
from CNN that were complete nonsequitors completely

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:27.320
ignoring what the candidates were actually
saying.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.320
Really embarrassing.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:35.020
And the biggest example of this was when they
asked Bernie about when he supposedly told

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:38.060
Elizabeth Warren a woman couldn't win.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.360
Bernie denied it.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.760
And they go right to Elizabeth Warren saying,
how did you feel when Bernie said a woman

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:44.920
couldn't win?

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.020
Bernie just denied it.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.340
And they skip over asking Elizabeth Warren.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.170
Well, Bernie denies it.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:51.170
Can you clarify?

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:52.170
Are you sure?

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.250
He said it was their context.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:54.250
Nothing.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.770
Look at this embarrassing moment from yesterday's
debate.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:03.031
CNN reported yesterday that and Senator Sanders,
Senator Warren confirmed it, a statement that

00:02:03.031 --> 00:02:07.630
in 2018 you told her that you did not believe
that a woman could win the election.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:09.420
Why did you say that?

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:13.090
Well, as a matter of fact, I didn't say it.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:16.230
Uh, and I don't want to waste a whole lot
of time on this because this is what Donald

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:19.819
Trump and maybe some of the media want.

00:02:19.819 --> 00:02:25.459
Anybody knows me, knows that it's incomprehensible
that I would think that a woman can not be

00:02:25.459 --> 00:02:26.650
president of the United States.

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:28.299
Go to YouTube today.

00:02:28.299 --> 00:02:32.900
There's some video of that of me 30 years
ago talking about how a woman could become

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:37.870
president of the United States in 2015 I deferred.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:43.760
In fact, the Senate award was a movement to
draft Senator Warren to run for president.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.980
And you know what I said, stayed back.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.129
Senator Warren decided not to run and I did.

00:02:49.129 --> 00:02:51.480
I did run afterwards.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:57.069
Hillary Clinton won the popular vote by 3
million votes.

00:02:57.069 --> 00:03:02.139
How could anybody in a million years not believe
that a woman could become president of the

00:03:02.139 --> 00:03:03.170
United States?

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:08.639
And let me be very clear if any of the women
on this stage or any of the men on this stage

00:03:08.639 --> 00:03:09.639
win the nomination.

00:03:09.639 --> 00:03:11.540
I hope that's not the case.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:18.499
But if they are, you will do everything in
my power to make sure that they are elected

00:03:18.499 --> 00:03:22.480
in order to the feet, the most dangerous president
in the history of our country.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:27.439
So Senator Sanders, Senator Sanders, I do
want to be clear here, yours

00:03:27.439 --> 00:03:32.019
saying that you never told Senator Warren
that a woman could not win the election.

00:03:32.019 --> 00:03:33.890
That is correct.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:37.959
Senator Warren, what did you think when Senator
Sandra Sanders told you a woman could not

00:03:37.959 --> 00:03:40.950
win the election?

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.340
I disagreed.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:43.840
Bernie says, I didn't say it.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.469
Next question is, Hey Elizabeth, what did
you think of of uh, what did you think of

00:03:47.469 --> 00:03:52.939
Bernie saying that this is not how you run
a debate and then afterwards they premised

00:03:52.939 --> 00:03:59.659
a full question round on it going to other
people with the title on screen saying, what

00:03:59.659 --> 00:04:03.159
do you say to people who think a woman can't
win the election?

00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:06.840
It's like who nobody has admitted to saying
that Bernie just denied.

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:12.500
Having said that, it was almost a Saturday
night live parody of what a debate would look

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:13.500
like.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.269
But unfortunately it was the actual debate.

00:04:15.269 --> 00:04:21.810
Now, by the way, not to Pat myself on the
back, but word for word, I called, how this

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:23.449
would go down two days ago.

00:04:23.449 --> 00:04:29.010
I tweeted on Monday prediction, when it comes
up tomorrow, Warren will refer to Bernie as

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:34.560
her friend and Bernie will say, of course
a woman can be president, but the moderators

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:36.069
will keep going.

00:04:36.069 --> 00:04:37.919
Check out what Elizabeth Warren said.

00:04:37.919 --> 00:04:40.160
I disagreed.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:44.490
Bernie is my friend and I am not here to try
to fight with Bernie.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:49.260
And then Bernie Sanders later getting the
opportunity to clarify and literally use the

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.009
words I tweeted on Monday.

00:04:51.009 --> 00:04:53.220
Of course a woman can be president.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.210
This is no big Pat on my back.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:05:01.090
It's that obvious how it would go and with
what CNN would try to do with it, we could

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:05.360
anticipate how Elizabeth Warren and Bernie
Sanders would handle it.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:08.520
Now on policy, there were some interesting
moments.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:12.560
The candidates were asked, would you bring
all troops home from the middle East?

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:13.810
No one said yes.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:15.550
And this tricked some people.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:19.680
Elizabeth Warren said she would bring all
combat troops home.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:22.229
That's playing coy with combat versus peacekeeping.

00:05:22.229 --> 00:05:23.229
Okay.

00:05:23.229 --> 00:05:26.289
And you have to understand that when I tweeted
about this last night, a few people wrote

00:05:26.289 --> 00:05:28.840
back and said, no, Warren said she would bring
everybody home.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:33.740
No, she said she would get combat troops out
of the region.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:37.000
That is way of not really answering the question.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.961
Bernie Sanders for example, a lot of people
thought, no, he, he said he would bring them

00:05:40.961 --> 00:05:42.170
all home.

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:47.800
Bernie Sanders listed things that we would
be better off having troops do than be in

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:52.129
the middle East, but Bernie also didn't say
that they would all come, come home and this

00:05:52.129 --> 00:05:54.060
is actually not shocking.

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:59.910
It would be unrealistic for a presidential
candidate who understands anything about geopolitics

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:05.810
to say every troop is coming home from the
middle East because the reality is some troops

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:09.550
are going to stay in some places in the middle
East, whether Bernie's president, whether

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:14.050
Warren's president, whether Biden's president
or whether Trump is reelected president.

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:15.389
That's just being realistic.

00:06:15.389 --> 00:06:19.740
But if you listen to how they said it, none
of them said they're all coming home.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:21.939
There was a discussion about healthcare costs.

00:06:21.939 --> 00:06:26.900
Bernie was asked about the price of his plan
and he was asked multiple times, don't we

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:29.280
